comment.narrative:
Five (05) CSOs have strengthened their representativeness and influence. It should be emphasized that among all the CSOs trained, some have strengthened their representativeness and influence in the constituencies and even at the national level, because they have used their skills and knowledge to achieve very satisfactory results on the following elements:
In 2024: (1)_Influence for the development and validation of the SYNERGIE Platform decree which establishes the institutional framework for dialogue between the Ministry of Sustainable Development, Transport and Housing and CSOs (pro-environment CSOs); (2) Influence for the updating/validation of the management action plans of the Ouémé and Mono biosphere reserves (CSOs = ACCB Chenal Gbaga; ACCB Tannou);
On the issues of influence and representativeness, some CSOs strengthened by Benkadi have performed well. It should be added that: (a) CSOs in the environment sector are more organized with better synergy of actions and more influence in environmental and climate governance in Benin; (b) The inclusive participation of CSOs in decision-making processes is institutionalized, through the revitalization of the MCVT institutional framework (with the implementation of Synergie Plus) and the strengthening of the APRM institutional framework (LOASAN and CNOS-CDeS and CCOS functionality); (c) A legal and regulatory environment favorable to the involvement of CSOs and inclusive citizen participation is put in place for a more effective preservation of natural ecosystems and a better conservation of biodiversity; (d) Enhanced collaboration and synergy of actions between all the partners involved in the project (sectoral ministries, parliamentarians, CSOs, local authorities, private sector).

